      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}.\n$$",
